son_id":"tvfy_10402","person_slug":"sandy-macdonald","vote":"no"},{"name":"Simon Birmingham","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10044","person_slug":"simon-birmingham","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Conroy","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10142","person_slug":"stephen-conroy","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Fielding","party":"Family First","person_id":"tvfy_10221","person_slug":"steve-fielding","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Hutchins","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10323","person_slug":"steve-hutchins","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sue Boyce","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10062","person_slug":"sue-boyce","vote":"no"},{"name":"Trish Crossin","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10161","person_slug":"trish-crossin","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Families, Community Services and Indigenous Affairs and Other Legislation Amendment (Northern Territory National Emergency Response and Other Measures) Bill 2007 - In Committee - Permit system and designated persons","noes":30,"question":"This division relates to the Policy _[For the NT National Emergency Response](/policies/36)_. The majority voted against [amendments](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?gid=2007-08-16.243.1) introduced by Labor Senator [Chris Evans](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Chris_Evans&mpc=Senate&house=senate), which means that it was rejected. The amendments relate to the permit system so as to \"allow access to roads and town community centres only to the class of people that we define in our amendments as 'designated persons'\".(Read Senator Evans' full explanation of his amendment [here](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?gid=2007-08-16.243.1). ) Senator Evans argued that this \"is a better balance between providing openness and transparency about what occurs in communities and the need for those communities to have their culture and tradition protected, and the security of the people who live in those communities assured\".(Read more about the changes to the permit system as proposed by the Government in the [bills digest](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/bd/bd0708/08bd021). ) _Background to the bills_ The [Families, Community Services and Indigenous Affairs and Other Legislation Amendment (Northern Territory National Emergency Response and Other Measures) Bill 2007](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/Result?bId=r2851) was introduced along with four other bills: - the [Social Security and Other Legislation Amendment (Welfare Payment Reform) Bill 2007](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/Result?bId=r2852) - the [Northern Territory National Emergency Response Bill 2007](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/Result?bId=r2850) - the [Appropriation (Northern Territory National Emergency Response) Bill (No. 1) 2007-2008](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Le","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-1405","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2007-08-16/9"}
